  "id": "fluctuating-asymmetry",
  "term": "fluctuating asymmetry",
  "definition": "Fluctuating asymmetry is small left-right unevenness in a trait, such as the face, that can occur normally and non-pathologically even in healthy people. In psychology-related research, it has been used as a possible marker of developmental instability, but the packet indicates that this use is limited and that it is not a generally sensitive indicator of stress.",
